course: dictionary
lesson: 1293
title: Buzz: sounds, feelings and names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Buzz has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Look at the words around it first. «The bee buzzed around the flowers» tells you that buzz is a sound and a movement, because bees move quickly and busily.
explain: «There was a buzz in the classroom» is different. There is no insect here, so buzz must mean an excited, busy feeling. Try your meaning in the sentence: «There was an excited, busy feeling in the classroom» still makes sense, so you have the right one.
explain: Capital letters give clues too. «Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin walked on the Moon» has a capital B because Buzz is a person's name. Always ask: does this word fit the meaning I think it has?
fact: Buzz can be a verb (to buzz) or a noun (a buzz).
fact: «Buzz» means a long, low humming sound, like a bee or a fly.
fact: «A buzz» can also mean an excited, busy feeling, as in «There was a buzz in the classroom.»
fact: «Give someone a buzz» is an informal way of saying to phone them.
fact: «Buzz off» is rude and means go away, so use it carefully.
exercise: «There was a buzz in the classroom.» What does buzz mean here? | A quiet, sleepy silence | A loud crash | *An excited, busy feeling | A bee stinging someone
exercise: «A rattlesnake buzzes its rattle.» What does buzzes mean? | Opens its mouth wide | *Makes a low humming sound | Moves very slowly | Bites someone hard
exercise: Jo says, «I'll give you a buzz when I get to the station.» What does give you a buzz mean? | *Phone you | Hum a tune to you | Let you into a building | Hit you gently
test: «Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin walked on the Moon.» What is Buzz in this sentence? | A busy, excited feeling | A sound a bee makes | A phone call | *A person's name
test: «You can feel the buzz on your throat» when you hum. What is the buzz? | A type of bone | *A low vibration you can feel | A cough | A tasty drink
exam: Mum says, «Buzz me in at the gate.» What does buzz mean? | *Press the buzzer so I can come in | Run away from the gate | Phone me when you get there | Walk around the garden quickly
